{
  "subtype": "focus_inference",
  "implied_focus": "Expense processing quality and spending magnitude — surfacing anomalies/risk in expense records (large amounts, processing delays, missing metadata, high-volume submitters)",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "amount_tier",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Buckets expense magnitude into Low/Medium/High, a directly actionable facet for flagging high-value spend worth scrutiny."
    },
    {
      "name": "processing_lag_days",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Quantifies delay between opening and processing, a process-quality facet an analyst can investigate for bottlenecks."
    },
    {
      "name": "missing_source_id",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Flags data-completeness/traceability gaps, a coherent facet of expense-record integrity and audit risk."
    },
    {
      "name": "submitter_expense_count",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Measures submitter activity/frequency, enabling detection of high-volume or anomalous submitters — relevant to spend oversight."
    }
  ],
  "focus_coherence": 0.72,
  "structure_quality": 0.7,
  "focus_actionability": 0.78,
  "rationale": "The four columns collectively cohere around auditing/analyzing expense records for what is 'worth analyzing and actionable': spend magnitude (amount_tier), process timeliness (processing_lag_days), data integrity (missing_source_id), and submitter behavior (submitter_expense_count). These are genuine, data-inferable analytical facets rather than mechanical text metrics, so they meaningfully realise an inferred focus. The main weakness is that the facets span somewhat distinct sub-themes (spend risk vs. data quality vs. process latency vs. submitter profiling), so the single-focus centering is moderate rather than tight — an analyst could reasonably see this as a broad 'expense audit health' framing rather than one sharply defined focus. Granularity is useful and non-trivial (tiers, counts, lag, flag), and the implied focus (identifying actionable/risky expense patterns) is clearly actionable, hence the reasonably high but not top scores."
}

